# Blaze cloud configuration.
#
# Copy this to `.env` in the same folder and fill in the real values. That file
# is gitignored and must stay that way: it holds a live database password.
#
# Anything already exported in the environment wins over this file, so a
# systemd unit or a one-off `$env:VAR = ...` in a terminal still overrides it.

# Supabase: Project Settings -> Database -> Connection string -> URI.
#
# Two things break this if you retype it by hand:
#   - Any % in the password must be written %25. A literal % is read as the
#     start of an escape and the connection fails with a confusing error.
#   - Use the SESSION POOLER host on port 5432, as below. The direct
#     db.<ref>.supabase.co host resolves to IPv6 only, so on a network without
#     IPv6 it does not fail — it hangs.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres

# Which address the API listens on. Loopback by default, which is right behind
# a reverse proxy. Set 0.0.0.0 to let another machine on the LAN reach it —
# needed when a second till is talking to a cloud running on this PC.
# BLAZE_CLOUD_HOST=0.0.0.0

# PORT=4000
